  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic and Social Infrastructure Program Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Economic and Social Infrastructure Program Phase 2 (ESIP2) is required to:  
- support the power and telecommunications sectors, including infrastructure delivery, capacity building and sectoral management  
- support the PNG Government to implement macro-level SOE reform, aimed at separating political and commercial decision-making, and help inform sound infrastructure planning and prioritisation, with a particular focus on power and telecommunications sectors  
- enable infrastructure delivery to contribute to the goals and objectives of other Australian sectoral programs, including security (as captured under the Bilateral Security Agreement &#x2013; BSA) and social infrastructure (including health and education infrastructure).  
The total value of this investment is planned to be $800m over 8 yrs.</narrative>
  </description>
